# Advisory session indicator

Branch: `session-indicator`, based on current root main
`5593932d5e8bc9fea2f52292fc0a5665b5c650a0` and Client main
`b5c3a7a5ddd37e010155883054931be3010fc5a2` (1.1.014).
Integrates root PR13, Client PR8 and Linux Host PR10 without replacing the
newer native camera, stereo microphone or audio-clock work.

## Contract

- Show In Session for a logged-in local desktop or reserved/live PLANK stream.
- Advisory only: same-user local-to-remote access, explicit remote takeover and
  different-user ownership enforcement are unchanged.
- Optional Linux/macOS username publication remains administrator-controlled and off
  by default. Opt-in exposes the sanitized name before authentication.
- No extra poll, account lookup, auth queue work or teardown from discovery.
- No persistent usernames in Client bookmarks. Preserve readable status while
  truncating long names. LoginWindow never publishes a remote user's name.

## Implementation

1. Retain the PR Client model/parser/UI work on top of current Client main.
   Reject names unless occupancy is exactly 1; preserve the status label width.
2. Reuse the account already resolved by the Linux supervisor. Bind its sanitized
   advisory name to the versioned private attachment record, and confirm the same
   UID/session/class against local logind before returning it. No new resolver,
   polling thread or service. Read stream occupancy atomically instead of calling
   the cleanup-producing session_count function.
3. Reflect macOS pending/active stream leases through an atomic advisory bit.
   Select pre-serialized occupied/free responses on the network queue; retain
   existing authentication and ownership policy without new locks or OS queries.
4. Test parser limits, privacy default, scope loss, login-screen streams, lease
   expiry/revocation, persistence absence and unchanged authentication behavior.
5. Run focused Linux and SDK27 checks from exact-source worktrees. Package builds
   and live desktop/takeover/UI acceptance remain separate gates. No deployment,
   release or merge to main without the corresponding operator request.

## Validation

Linux production occupancy and private-record tests pass locally, including
10000 cached reads, name limits, malformed records and desktop transitions.
Existing session-policy tests and supervisor GCC14/C++23 compilation pass.
The production stream owner is exercised with stub media workers: reservations,
failed/successful setup, removal and status polling during a deliberately stalled
join all pass. SDK27 authentication/discovery, TLS loopback and certificate-chain
tests pass. Actual Qt Client parser/persistence tests and QML syntax pass on the
Ubuntu builder. See HANDOFF for exact source provenance and the unrelated stale
packaging source-pattern assertions. Full package, visual UI and live session
qualification remain pending; no installed software was changed.

## Follow-up: optional remembered sign-in username (issue17)

Implemented on this branch, without changing Host authentication or the public
occupancy contract. Administrator policy `authentication.remember_username`
defaults false on Linux/macOS Clients. Store only the successful local sign-in
name per bookmark, never discovery usernames, passwords or tokens. Prefill an
editable field and focus the password, without auto-submit. Clear names when
destinations change; disabling policy purges primary and backup entries at
startup. Preserve the current same-user access and takeover rules.

Production policy/parser/persistence tests and the actual inline login dialog
run offscreen on the Ubuntu builder. All pass; package and live-session tests
remain separate. Documentation: `docs/user/remembered-usernames.md`.

## Follow-up: macOS Host settings (issue20)

Expose `[security] publish_session_user = false` and `[network] ping_timeout =
10000` in the macOS INI reader and fully commented reference template. Reuse the
desktop provisioning account lookup, sanitize/cache the short name only after
administrator opt-in, and never publish an authenticated remote name at
LoginWindow. Existing graphical-worker retirement handles logout/user switching;
locking keeps the same desktop scope. No discovery-time resolver or new service.

Pass the validated 200–120000 ms inactivity limit into native QUIC; preserve
the existing one-second keepalive at the default and shorten it for smaller
timeouts. Keep the independent 10-second handshake deadline and Client
Wait/Disconnect policy unchanged. Reject invalid Mac INI values, test boundary
values and upgrade preservation, and correct Linux's legacy media-ping comments
without changing Linux runtime behavior. Existing Client metadata-v1 parsing
already handles optional Mac names; no new feature bit or fallback is needed.

## Follow-up: automatic macOS workstation name (issue19)

When `[general] host_name` is absent, resolve the local OS hostname at startup
through `gethostname()`, matching Linux. Validate length/UTF-8/control characters;
fall back to `PLANK` if the OS lookup fails or returns unusable data. Explicit
administrator overrides always win. Do not add DNS queries, per-poll lookups,
another preference source, a watcher or an install-time hostname snapshot.

Ship a fully documented commented-out override. Retire only the exact old
installer-generated INI name block, with validated ownership/mode/content and
an atomic replacement; retain all other bytes and preserve edited/custom blocks.
The existing one-time plist conversion omits the old generic placeholder and
still retains custom names, ports, UUID and TLS material. Validate defaults,
hostname changes/failure, custom overrides, idempotent upgrades, interrupted
installation, and rejection of unsafe files before any configuration rewrite.
No Client runtime, protocol, authentication or Linux behavior change is needed.
